13. COMMAND VALIDATION
Before execution, commands shall be validated at three levels.
Structural validation
Checks:
required fields
types
UUID validity
enumerations
parameter formats
Domain validation
Checks:
object existence
object compatibility
relationship validity
model rules
project state
Constraint validation
Checks:
active constraints
geometric constraints
regulatory constraints
coordination constraints
document dependencies
A command that fails validation shall not mutate the project.

14. OPTIMISTIC CONCURRENCY
OneDraft shall use optimistic concurrency for model mutations.
Each command may specify:
expected_revision
expected_model_version
The service compares those values against current state.
If they differ:
REVISION_CONFLICT
shall be returned.
This prevents an operation created against an obsolete model state from silently overwriting newer work.

15. TRANSACTION SERVICE
The ProjectModelService established in the previous implementation stage becomes the primary transactional boundary.
Conceptually:
with project_transaction(context):
    state = repository.load(context.project_id)

    validate_command(state, command)

    result = domain.execute(state, command)

    repository.persist(result)

    revision = revision_service.create(result)

    event_service.record(result)

    transaction.commit()
The implementation shall guarantee atomicity of the relational model update.

