44. EVENT RULE
Events shall never be emitted as successful completion signals before the associated transaction has committed.
The sequence is:
TRANSACTION
 ↓
COMMIT
 ↓
EVENT PUBLICATION
This prevents external consumers from observing a state that was subsequently rolled back.

45. OUTBOX PATTERN
To preserve reliable event publication, OneDraft shall use an outbox pattern.
Within the same database transaction:
MODEL CHANGE
+
OUTBOX EVENT
are committed together.
A background publisher then sends the event to the event system.
This prevents the failure condition:
DATABASE COMMIT
+
EVENT LOST

