49. RETRY POLICY
Retries shall be permitted only for operations classified as retry-safe.
Transient infrastructure failures may be retried.
Domain validation failures shall not be retried automatically.
Examples of retryable conditions:
temporary database connection failure
temporary object-storage failure
temporary queue failure
temporary AI provider failure
Examples of non-retryable conditions:
invalid geometry
constraint conflict
revision conflict
authorization failure
invalid command
failed mandatory validation

50. AI RETRY POLICY
AI requests shall receive deterministic execution identifiers where practical.
A retry must not automatically execute a previously proposed command twice.
The sequence remains:
AI RESPONSE
 ↓
COMMAND IDENTIFICATION
 ↓
COMMAND VALIDATION
 ↓
COMMAND EXECUTION

